## IBM / Mike Cowlishaw "General Decimal Arithmetic Testcases" v2.62

The `BigDecimal` conformance tests reproduce a subset of the official test
suite published at https://speleotrove.com/decimal/dectest.html:

  * inline in `src/big.zig`'s test blocks — add.decTest, multiply.decTest,
    quantize.decTest, divide.decTest, rounding.decTest
  * extracted mechanically into `src/testdata/*.vec` — remainder.decTest,
    min.decTest, max.decTest, squareroot.decTest, power.decTest

Test IDs are kept for traceability, and each `.vec` file repeats the notice in
its own header. The suite's terms:

    Reproduced with permission ...
    Copyright (c) 1997, 2009 by International Business Machines Corporation

Only test-case text is reproduced. The implementation under test is the
authors' own (MIT), built on `std.math.big.int`; its DESIGN references (Java
`BigDecimal`, the IBM General Decimal Arithmetic specification, the Python
`decimal` docs) are recorded in the repository NOTICE §2 as provenance, not as
a condition.
